+    <div class="sect3">
+     <h4 id="storage_volume_types">
+      7.2.3. Volume Types of Guests
+      <a class="headerlink" href="#storage_volume_types" title="Permalink to this heading">
+      </a>
+     </h4>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       The content types
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        images
+       </span>
+       and
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        rootdir
+       </span>
+       allow all volumes of VMs or of
+containers on a storage. To allow only some of them, set the specific volume
+types as content types instead.
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div style="overflow-x:auto">
+      <table class="tableblock frame-all grid-all" style="
+width:100%;
+">
+       <caption class="title">
+        Table 3. Content types for the volumes of guests
+       </caption>
+       <col style="width:20%;"/>
+       <col style="width:20%;"/>
+       <col style="width:60%;"/>
+       <thead>
+        <tr>
+         <th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          Content type
+         </th>
+         <th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          Web interface
+         </th>
+         <th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          Allows
+         </th>
+        </tr>
+       </thead>
+       <tbody>
+        <tr>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock monospaced">
+           images
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           Disk image
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           All volumes of VMs:
+           <span class="monospaced">
+            vm-vol
+           </span>
+           and
+           <span class="monospaced">
+            vm-state
+           </span>
+          </p>
+         </td>
+        </tr>
+        <tr>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock monospaced">
+           vm-vol
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           VM Disk
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           Disks of VMs, including EFI disks, TPM states and
+cloud-init drives
+          </p>
+         </td>
+        </tr>
+        <tr>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock monospaced">
+           vm-state
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           VM State
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           Saved states of VMs, from snapshots that include
+the RAM and from hibernation
+          </p>
+         </td>
+        </tr>
+        <tr>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock monospaced">
+           rootdir
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           Container
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           All volumes of containers, which currently is only
+           <span class="monospaced">
+            ct-vol
+           </span>
+          </p>
+         </td>
+        </tr>
+        <tr>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock monospaced">
+           ct-vol
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           Container Volume
+          </p>
+         </td>
+         <td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top">
+          <p class="tableblock">
+           Root disks and mount points of containers
+          </p>
+         </td>
+        </tr>
+       </tbody>
+      </table>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       Existing storages do not need to be changed. Use the volume types if a storage
+should hold only some of the volumes of guests. For example, to keep the saved
+states of VMs off a storage that is used for VM disks and containers:
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="listingblock">
+      <div class="content monospaced">
+       <pre># pvesm set &lt;STORAGE_ID&gt; --content vm-vol,rootdir</pre>
+      </div>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       Or to add a directory storage that only holds the saved states of VMs:
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="listingblock">
+      <div class="content monospaced">
+       <pre># pvesm add dir vmstate --path /mnt/vmstate --content vm-state</pre>
+      </div>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       In the web interface, tick
+       <em>
+        Advanced
+       </em>
+       in the dialog for adding or editing a
+storage. The
+       <em>
+        Content
+       </em>
+       selector then also lists the volume types. Select
+       <em>
+        VM Disk
+       </em>
+       or
+       <em>
+        VM State
+       </em>
+       instead of
+       <em>
+        Disk image
+       </em>
+       , or
+       <em>
+        Container Volume
+       </em>
+       instead
+of
+       <em>
+        Container
+       </em>
+       . A volume type has no effect next to the content type that
+already allows it, for example
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        vm-vol
+       </span>
+       next to
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        images
+       </span>
+       , and is dropped from
+the configuration.
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       Where the state of a VM is saved if the storages of its disks do not allow
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        vm-state
+       </span>
+       is described for the
+       <a href="#qm_vmstatestorage">
+        <span class="monospaced">
+         vmstatestorage
+        </span>
+       </a>
+       option.
+      </p>
+     </div>
