+        <td class="content">
+         If you extend a shared volume group onto another device on one node, the
+other nodes may only see the added physical volume after LVM has scanned their
+devices again, for example with
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          pvscan --cache
+         </span>
+         . This command also resets the
+autoactivation records of LVM, which can let LVM activate logical volumes on its
+own later. Proxmox VE disables autoactivation for the logical volumes it creates.
+Before you run the command, make sure that autoactivation is also disabled for
+all other logical volumes of the volume group, for example with
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          lvchange --setautoactivation n &lt;vg&gt;/&lt;lv&gt;
+         </span>
+         . Proxmox VE runs the same rescan on its
+own when it does not find the volume group of a storage at all, so keep
+autoactivation disabled for all logical volumes of a shared volume group.
