+      <div class="sect5">
+       <h6 id="pveceph_cephx_other_users">
+        Ceph Users Not Managed by Proxmox VE
+        <a class="headerlink" href="#pveceph_cephx_other_users" title="Permalink to this heading">
+        </a>
+       </h6>
        <div class="paragraph">
         <p>
-         The helper lists local users not managed by Proxmox VE separately. Follow their
-client’s supported rotation procedure, or leave their keys unchanged and keep
-the old cipher enabled.
+         The helper lists local users not managed by Proxmox VE separately, as keys that
+need manual migration. Follow their client’s supported rotation procedure, or
+leave their keys unchanged and keep the old cipher enabled.
+        </p>
+       </div>
+       <div class="paragraph">
+        <p>
+         If every client of such a user supports
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          aes256k
+         </span>
+         , move the clients to a new
+user with an
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          aes256k
+         </span>
+         key. Both users work side by side, so each client can
+switch when convenient, for example one node of a Kubernetes cluster using
+Ceph CSI at a time. For a user
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          client.app
+         </span>
+         with RBD access to the pool
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          vm-pool
+         </span>
+         :
+        </p>
+       </div>
+       <div class="olist arabic">
+        <ol class="arabic">
+         <li>
+          <p>
+           Show the capabilities of the current user:
+          </p>
+          <div class="listingblock">
+           <div class="content">
+            <!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight
+by Lorenzo Bettini
+http://www.lorenzobettini.it
+http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
+            <pre><tt>ceph auth get client<span style="color: #990000">.</span>app</tt></pre>
+           </div>
+          </div>
+         </li>
+         <li>
+          <p>
+           Create the new user with the same capabilities and an
+           <span class="monospaced">
+            aes256k
+           </span>
+           key:
+          </p>
+          <div class="listingblock">
+           <div class="content">
+            <!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight
+by Lorenzo Bettini
+http://www.lorenzobettini.it
+http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
+            <pre><tt>ceph auth get-or-create client<span style="color: #990000">.</span>app2 mon <span style="color: #FF0000">'profile rbd'</span> <span style="color: #990000">\</span>
+    osd <span style="color: #FF0000">'profile rbd pool=vm-pool'</span> --key-type<span style="color: #990000">=</span>aes256k</tt></pre>
+           </div>
+          </div>
+         </li>
+         <li>
+          <p>
+           Transfer the printed keyring securely and configure every client to use the
+  new user.
+          </p>
+         </li>
+         <li>
+          <p>
+           Once a dry run of the helper with
+           <span class="monospaced">
+            --restrict-ciphers
+           </span>
+           lists no client
+  connected as
+           <span class="monospaced">
+            client.app
+           </span>
+           any more, delete that user:
+          </p>
+          <div class="listingblock">
+           <div class="content">
+            <!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight
+by Lorenzo Bettini
+http://www.lorenzobettini.it
+http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
+            <pre><tt>ceph auth del client<span style="color: #990000">.</span>app</tt></pre>
+           </div>
+          </div>
+         </li>
+        </ol>
+       </div>
+       <div class="paragraph">
+        <p>
+         Alternatively, you can rotate the key in place with
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          ceph auth rotate --key-type=aes256k &lt;USER&gt;
+         </span>
+         <span class="footnote">
+          <br/>
+          [Ceph key rotation
+          <a href="https://docs.ceph.com/en/latest/rados/configuration/auth-config-ref/#upgrading-and-rotating-cephx-keys">
+           https://docs.ceph.com/en/latest/rados/configuration/auth-config-ref/#upgrading-and-rotating-cephx-keys
+          </a>
+          ]
+          <br/>
+         </span>
+         .
+This replaces the key at once, without the grace period of a staged key.
+Transfer the printed keyring securely, update every saved copy and refresh the
+clients.
+        </p>
+       </div>
+       <div class="paragraph">
+        <p>
+         If an earlier helper run with
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          --apply
+         </span>
+         recorded the previous key, the helper
+then asks you to confirm the refresh with
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          --confirm-clients-refreshed &lt;USER&gt; --apply
+         </span>
+         . The first confirmation may only
+record which clients are connected. In that case, repeat the command.
         </p>
        </div>
       </div>
