+/F/lgJiyQFHragAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="/>
+        </td>
+        <td class="content">
+         The policy is enforced by the nodes that handle a token request,
+so in a cluster, only configure it once all nodes run a version supporting
+it. Nodes running an older version ignore the policy, and changing
+datacenter options on such a node removes it from the configuration.
+        </td>
+       </tr>
+      </table>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       Changing the policy requires
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        Sys.Modify
+       </span>
+       on
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        /
+       </span>
+       , like any other datacenter
+option. Configure it in the web interface under
+       <strong>
+        Datacenter → Options →
+API Token Policy
+       </strong>
+       , or on the command line:
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="listingblock">
+      <div class="content">
+       <!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight
+by Lorenzo Bettini
+http://www.lorenzobettini.it
+http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
+       <pre><tt>pvesh <span style="font-weight: bold"><span style="color: #0000FF">set</span></span> /cluster/options --token-policy max-lifetime<span style="color: #990000">=</span><span style="color: #993399">7776000</span></tt></pre>
+      </div>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        max-lifetime
+       </span>
+       is set in seconds (7776000 above is 90 days), while the web
+interface takes days. It counts from when the expiration date is set, that
+is on token creation or when an update changes it, and implies
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        require-expiry
+       </span>
+       , as a token without an expiration date would exceed any
+maximum lifetime.
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       The policy only applies when a token is created or updated, and only to
+values that actually change. Existing tokens stay valid even if they do not
+conform to a policy configured later, and unrelated updates of such tokens
+keep working. A new expiration date must be within the limit. With
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        disallow-expiry-extension
+       </span>
+       , the expiration date of an existing token can
+only be shortened, or set if it has none. Tokens can always be deleted and
+recreated.
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       With
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        allow-extension-on-regenerate
+       </span>
+       , an existing token can still be
+extended within the limit when its secret is regenerated in the same
+request. The old secret stops working, like it would when recreating the
+token, so tools can rotate their tokens in place without setting up the
+permissions again. In the web interface, enable
+       <strong>
+        Regenerate Secret
+       </strong>
+       in the
+token edit dialog and set the new expiration date. On the command line, pass
+the new expiration date in Unix epoch seconds:
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="listingblock">
+      <div class="content">
+       <!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight
+by Lorenzo Bettini
+http://www.lorenzobettini.it
+http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
+       <pre><tt>pveum user token modify <span style="color: #990000">&lt;</span>userid<span style="color: #990000">&gt;</span> <span style="color: #990000">&lt;</span>tokenid<span style="color: #990000">&gt;</span> --expire <span style="color: #990000">&lt;</span>timestamp<span style="color: #990000">&gt;</span> --regenerate <span style="color: #993399">1</span></tt></pre>
+      </div>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       Like on creation, the new secret is only displayed once, so update the tool
+to use it right away.
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="admonitionblock">
+      <table>
+       <tr>
+        <td class="icon">
+         <img alt="Note" src="data:image/png;base64,
+iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAADAAAAAwCAYAAABXAvmHAAAJhUlEQVRoge2ZWWycVxXHf+fce7/v
