+         The policy also applies to tokens that other tools create through the
+API, for example when adding the cluster as a remote to Proxmox Datacenter
+Manager. For tools that do not set an expiration date, set
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          default-to-max-lifetime
+         </span>
+         together with
+         <span class="monospaced">
+          max-lifetime
+         </span>
+         , so that their tokens
+get the maximum lifetime instead of being rejected. If a tool still cannot
+create a compliant token, for example because it disables privilege
+separation, create one manually and use that in the tool instead.
